       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer. The problem is the dose, not whether you meant it. 1000 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of 200 mg. It could seriously harm the patient with serotonin syndrome, seizures, or dangerous heart rhythm changes. I also can't treat a confirmation from a non-prescriber as clinical authorization.\n\nIf there is a clinical reason for this dose, the right route is:\n- **The treating prescriber** enters the order directly or tells me the intended dose.\n- **Pharmacy** reviews the order. They can check it against the patient's chart and indication.\n\nIf the prescriber wants a standard dose, I can enter it right away. Typical adult dosing is 25\u2013200 mg once daily. Tell me the dose and the indication, and I'll enter it."
